"""Ascend-specialized multi_margin_loss backward.

The generic implementation launches one Ascend program per row and walks the
class dimension in fixed 256-wide blocks. On an NPU that leaves most vector
cores idle for small batches (``grid == N``), re-reads the target value once
per class block and pays a synchronous target-range check (kernel launch +
``.item()``) on every new target tensor.

The kernel below tiles *rows* as well as classes: one program owns
``BLOCK_N`` whole rows, so a row is touched exactly once and the class loop
collapses into a single vectorized block whenever ``C <= 4096``. The
target-column gradient (-sum of the other columns) is produced in the same
program, so the backward pass needs exactly one launch. Out-of-range targets
are clamped to class 0 instead of being validated with a host sync; the
generic ``flag_gems.ops.multi_margin_loss`` keeps the strict check.
"""

